.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-api - Call Microsoft Graph directly


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams api   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Call a Graph endpoint directly, for the operations the CLI does not wrap.

.PP
 is an HTTP method (GET, POST, PATCH, PUT, DELETE) and  is a
Graph path such as /me or /teams/{id}/channels; it may carry a query string.

.PP
Fields:
  -f key=value   a string field, dotted keys nest (body.content=hi)
  -F key=value   a typed field: true, false, null and numbers keep their type
  --input     the whole JSON body from a file, or - for stdin

.PP
Read-only mode refuses every method but GET and HEAD.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print the request without sending it

.PP
\fB-f\fP, \fB--field\fP=[]
	add a string field to the JSON body (key=value, dotted keys nest)

.PP
\fB--header\fP=[]
	extra request header ("Name: value", repeatable)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for api

.PP
\fB--input\fP=""
	read the JSON body from a file, or - for stdin

.PP
\fB--query\fP=[]
	query parameter (key=value, repeatable)

.PP
\fB-F\fP, \fB--raw-field\fP=[]
	add a typed field (true/false, a number and null keep their type)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams(1)\fP
